### Renter: log in, find a car, request it, view it and cancel it
### Start the server first: .\kotlin.bat run -m server
### Daan is a demo user (see DemoData.kt)

### Log in and save the token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "daan@example.com",
  "password": "Welkom123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("renterToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Log in with a wrong password (401)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "daan@example.com",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### Find an electric car in Breda
GET http://localhost:8080/api/cars?type=BEV&city=Breda

### Request the Tesla (car 4) for 4 hours
POST http://localhost:8080/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{renterToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "carId": 4,
  "start": "2030-01-10T09:00",
  "end": "2030-01-10T13:00",
  "expectedKm": 80
}

> {%
    client.global.set("reservationId", response.body.id);
%}

### A reservation of only 30 minutes (400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{renterToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "carId": 4,
  "start": "2030-01-11T09:00",
  "end": "2030-01-11T09:30",
  "expectedKm": 10
}

### My reservations
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{renterToken}}

### One reservation (after approval it shows the contact details of the owner)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{renterToken}}

### Try to approve my own request (403: only the owner can do this)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{renterToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "APPROVED"
}

### Cancel the reservation
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{renterToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CANCELLED"
}
